Ladybird loads the document a use element refers to as a resource
document of its own, apart from images, and takes any well-formed XML
document, whatever its root element. The other engines do the same.
Blink loads it as an SVGResourceDocumentContent, which SVGUseElement
looks its target up in, and WebKit’s CachedSVGDocument::finishLoading()
parses it into an SVGDocument with no frame. Gecko loads it into the
external resource map of the use element’s document, with
ExternalResourceMap::RequestResource(). None of them needs an svg root.
